# 10. Fix round after the reviewer's `changes` on f96ad6be20d
# Three blocking findings from the reviewer (agent-vitana-lane-reviewer-202611052248-7739): (1) bootstrap_admin_user (R2) is
# SECURITY DEFINER with no REVOKE from PUBLIC and anon and no definer-public reason, which fails
# services/gateway/test/vtid-05041-definer-lockdown.test.ts (the rule at lines 125-137); (2) the rollback (R3) has the same gap;
# (3) no gateway Jest ran on this supabase-only PR, so npm run test:roles was unevidenced.
$ cd services/gateway && npm ci   -> added 850 packages, exit 0 (gateway dependencies were absent in this worktree)
$ npx jest test/vtid-05041-definer-lockdown.test.ts   (on f96ad6be20d, before the fix) -> outputs/jest-vtid-05041-before-fix.txt:
  1 failed (the SECURITY DEFINER rule), 6 passed, 1 skipped
Fix:
  - 20261102033100 (R2): REVOKE ALL ON FUNCTION public.bootstrap_admin_user(uuid, text) FROM PUBLIC, anon, authenticated;
    GRANT EXECUTE ON FUNCTION public.bootstrap_admin_user(uuid, text) TO service_role; the self-check raises if anon or
    authenticated can execute it. The header now names the grant change.
  - 20261102033000_role_source_rollback (R3): a `-- definer-public:` reason. The file has no GRANT or REVOKE statement.
    CREATE OR REPLACE keeps each function's ACL, so the rollback does not reopen bootstrap_admin_user. Restoring PUBLIC
    EXECUTE would re-expose it, against the S2 rule.
  - supabase/tests/mt_identity_roles_bootstrap.test.sql: plan 20 -> 24. Assertions 21-24 check anon, authenticated, PUBLIC
    and service_role. They fail on the previous body and pass after apply.
  - docs/validation/VTID-05467/pglite-check.mjs: the rollback check compares the catalog exactly except bootstrap's ACL, which
    it checks by its end state. The first run failed there, as designed (the ACL differs from base). The second run failed on
    a lookup bug: regprocedure::text omits the schema for functions on the search path. The lookup now matches on the name.
$ node run.mjs <worktree>   (PGlite; copy of pglite-check.mjs in /projects/sandbox/pglite-05467)
  -> ALL CHECKS PASSED. Red base: R1 13 of 28 failing; R2 16 of 24 failing, including assertions 21-23.
     After apply and after re-apply: R1 28/28, R2 24/24. Rollback on base: fingerprint identical.
     Rollback after a switch: catalog identical except the bootstrap ACL, which is {postgres=X/postgres,service_role=X/postgres}.
     Negative control: 8 failing assertions (expected). Id variant: red, then pass.
$ npm run test:roles   -> outputs/jest-test-roles.txt: Tests 105 passed, 105 total, exit 0
$ npx jest test/vtid-05041-definer-lockdown.test.ts   -> outputs/jest-vtid-05041.txt: 7 passed, 1 skipped, exit 0
  The skipped case runs the SQL harness (scripts/ci/test-vtid-05041-definer-lockdown.sh), which needs a local PostgreSQL
